        "id": 40557,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-19T13:29:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Once you have Master of Magic out …</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This is the key, I think. With Master of Magic out, Nightmist is ready to rock and is quite powerful, but perhaps the most interesting thing about Nightmist is when Master of Magic is <em>NOT</em> out, giving the player the interesting choice of whether to focus on getting Master of Magic or focusing on contributing directly to the battle.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
