        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/9fc348/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-19T15:11:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"lugaru\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lugaru/48/2767_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lugaru:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, when I played the game originally I was like \"I love how simple this system is, but I fear there is not much they can do with it\".Nightmist challenges that a little by being very flexible yet straightforward, and I agree that she is more fun before you get Master, but if you want to actually WIN it is a good idea to get it out early… there is no prize for fighting with one hand behind your back.&nbsp;Btw… I love flipping her deck and trash&nbsp;so almost everything is in the trash and then using that to heal her… I forget the card names for that combo but it is great.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Mists of Time + Mistbound Recovery <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
